    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This contribution presents a methodology for visualizing fault segmentation and shale smearing using 3-D seismic data from the Niger delta. The seismic data have been recently reprocessed and show clear segmentation of the normal fault under study. Well data and stratigraphic mapping compliment the visualization of shale-smearing in the fault zones. This approach enables the interpretation of subtle features such as normal fault segmentation and especially the associated smearing of shale layers into the fault zone in the Niger delta. The fault under study appears as discontinuous segments whose relay zones are the locations of smeared shale units. It is expected that these techniques will improve the evaluation of the capacity of fault seals which have developed from the smearing of shale layers into the fault zones.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
